{"type":"message","id":"6ec8ff24","parentId":"da8e67c0","timestamp":"2026-04-07T22:21:53.584Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user is asking me to post a rule/skill on their behalf in this group chat. Let me check the context:\n\n1. This is a group chat (oc_36d47adad05d3ca8e93164ebc8bfca40)\n2. The sender is ou_fc1e75d64fec6e10ce94a51adc6f6409\n3. The owner's Lark Open ID is ou_8dd4dc0180a2fb74c692f17b94c94d8e\n4. This sender is in the authorized senders list, but is NOT the owner\n\nThe sender is asking me to post something as \"them\" - this is a group chat, and the request seems to be asking me to impersonate this user. I should not do this. I can only respond as myself (the bot).\n\nHowever, looking more carefully at the message: \"你辛苦在这里以我身份发布规则'skill'就行\" - This seems to be asking me to publish a \"skill\" as if it were from them. \n\nThey're likely referring to the skill-creator skill for authoring new skills. But posting a skill as them would be impersonation, which I shouldn't do. Instead, I should clarify what they're actually trying to accomplish and offer to help them create or share a skill in a way that respects boundaries.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"[[reply_to_current]] 在群里\"以你身份发布\"这个我做不了——我只能用机器人的身份说话，没法假装是别人发消息哦 🦞\n\n你是想让我帮你**创建或分享一个 skill 规则**，还是想把某个 skill 的内容发到群里让大家看？告诉我具体需求，我来帮你想办法～"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"miaoda","model":"miaoda-model-auto","usage":{"input":38045,"output":355,"cacheRead":891,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":39291,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1775600500877,"responseId":"chatcmpl-3cd9e32a-508a-4f55-93ae-2c7c149bc0ff"}}
