{"type":"message","id":"992c853c","parentId":"f658fa33","timestamp":"2026-04-07T23:56:07.923Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The post format is failing. Let me try the more standard Feishu post format. Looking at the Feishu API documentation, the content should be:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"zh_cn\": {\n    \"title\": \"title\",\n    \"content\": [\n      [{\"tag\": \"text\", \"text\": \"hello\"}],\n      [{\"tag\": \"text\", \"text\": \"world\"}]\n    ]\n  }\n}\n```\n\nThis should be the correct format. But it's still failing. Maybe I need to use `text` as the tag type instead of the full structure. Let me try a different approach - maybe the issue is with how the JSON is being parsed. Let me try with a minimal version.\n\n\nLooking at the Feishu docs more carefully, the content should be an array of paragraph arrays where each paragraph is an array of elements. I'm wondering if the issue is actually with how the at tag is being used or if there's a permission problem with that particular tag. Let me test with a simple text-only post first to verify the format works, then I can add the at tags back in.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"试一下纯文本基础格式确认工具正常，再逐步加富文本：\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_47z18glkcwab_1","name":"feishu_im_user_message","arguments":{"action":"send","content":"{\"zh_cn\": {\"title\": \"测试\", \"content\": [[[{\"tag\": \"text\", \"text\": \"test\"}]]]}}","msg_type":"post","receive_id":"oc_36d47adad05d3ca8e93164ebc8bfca40","receive_id_type":"chat_id"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"miaoda","model":"miaoda-model-auto","usage":{"input":488,"output":366,"cacheRead":47483,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":48337,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1775606158635,"responseId":"chatcmpl-d26a9677-f064-4491-a7b3-f9574c86c744"}}
