{"type":"message","id":"62a1466c","parentId":"18b008fc","timestamp":"2026-04-07T23:57:28.383Z","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"System: [2026-04-08 07:57:27 GMT+8] Feishu[default] group oc_36d47adad05d3ca8e93164ebc8bfca40 | ou_fc1e75d64fec6e10ce94a51adc6f6409 [msg:om_x100b526dd0aad0a0c454657a03b5ff2, reply_to:om_x100b526dd593eca4b2e3a5264aa4c88, @bot]\n\nConversation info (untrusted metadata):\n```json\n{\n  \"message_id\": \"om_x100b526dd0aad0a0c454657a03b5ff2\",\n  \"sender_id\": \"ou_fc1e75d64fec6e10ce94a51adc6f6409\",\n  \"conversation_label\": \"oc_36d47adad05d3ca8e93164ebc8bfca40\",\n  \"sender\": \"ou_fc1e75d64fec6e10ce94a51adc6f6409\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"Wed 2026-04-08 07:57 GMT+8\",\n  \"group_subject\": \"oc_36d47adad05d3ca8e93164ebc8bfca40\",\n  \"is_group_chat\": true,\n  \"was_mentioned\": true,\n  \"has_reply_context\": true\n}\n```\n\nSender (untrusted metadata):\n```json\n{\n  \"label\": \"ou_fc1e75d64fec6e10ce94a51adc6f6409\",\n  \"id\": \"ou_fc1e75d64fec6e10ce94a51adc6f6409\",\n  \"name\": \"ou_fc1e75d64fec6e10ce94a51adc6f6409\"\n}\n```\n\nReplied message (untrusted, for context):\n```json\n{\n  \"body\": \"[message_id=om_x100b526dd593eca4b2e3a5264aa4c88] 发出去了！✅ 这次用了 text + @_user_ 特殊语法实现@各AI伙伴。\\n不过 post 富文本格式（bold、颜色等）报错，工具暂时不支持——目前能做到：\\n- ✅ text 消息带 @*user* 格式@人\\n- ❌ post 富文本 bold/颜色（待排查）\\n要更新 skill 里把这条@规范记下来吗？顺便记录一下 text 格式的@语法。\"\n}\n```\n\n第一，你的这个“@”还是文本字符不会起到激活作用，第二个呢，你要艾特他们的飞书的名称，而不是ID，你可以通过ID找到他了，但是你@id他们无法收到消息"}],"timestamp":1775606248373}}
{"type":"message","id":"78613217","parentId":"62a1466c","timestamp":"2026-04-07T23:57:42.234Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user is saying:\n1. The `@_user_ou_xxx` format is just text characters and won't actually @ those users - they won't receive notifications\n2. I need to @ them by their Lark display name (nickname), not their ID\n\nThe problem is that the `feishu_im_user_message` tool with text type doesn't support actual @mentions that trigger notifications. The post type format also failed.\n\nFor actual @mentions that work, I need to use the `interactive` (card) type message, or use the `feishu_im_user_message` with a special format. But neither seems to be working.\n \nNow I'm realizing the `feishu_im_user_message` tool actually does support proper @mention syntax in the `at` tag within post messages - that's what enables real user notifications. Let me check why the post format failed and try a different approach, maybe looking at how the bot identity handles this differently than the user identity tool.\n\nThe user identity tool is returning \"invalid message content\" which suggests the content parameter format itself might be the issue. Let me try structuring the post content in the specific format that works, or reconsider whether I should be using the bot identity for this group message instead.\n\nActually, I'm realizing the core constraint: the bot can send messages but can't mention users in a way that triggers notifications, while the user identity tool supports @mentions but has issues with the post format. The best path forward might be to use the user identity tool with a properly formatted post structure that includes at-mentions, since that would actually notify the mentioned users.\n\nI'm trying to construct the JSON content for the post message with at-mentions...\n\nConstructing the message content...","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"明白了！让我排查一下 post 格式问题。text 里的 @_user_ 确实是纯文本，不会触发通知。必须用 post 富文本格式的 `at` 标签才能真正@到人。\n\n让我找到正确格式再发：\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_5le5142954wb_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"find /home/gem/workspace/agent/extensions/openclaw-lark -name \"*.js\" -o -name \"*.ts\" 2>/dev/null | head -20"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_5le5142954wb_2","name":"feishu_im_user_message","arguments":{"action":"send","content":"{\"text\": \"测试消息\"}","msg_type":"text","receive_id":"oc_36d47adad05d3ca8e93164ebc8bfca40","receive_id_type":"chat_id"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"miaoda","model":"miaoda-model-auto","usage":{"input":3169,"output":557,"cacheRead":45691,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":49417,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1775606248383,"responseId":"chatcmpl-7abafb39-4ebe-4d1c-9385-30732f0861eb"}}
